{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (40%) to Halictine 2. L: 22%; M=N=K: 11%. Discovered from the human unconventional myosin 1h protein by computer prediction. Activity: weakly active against S.aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC 128 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 64 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 64 uM). In vitro Toxicity: human RBC: HC50 >128 uM. not hemo.lytic. Structure: it became helical after binding to lipids. More helical in the presence of anionic DMPG (85.9%) than DMPC (40.3%).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31386688", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2019 Aug 6;14(8):e0220656. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0220656. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03769", "source_id": "AP03769", "source_numeric_id": "03769", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03769", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Intragenic antimicrobial peptides (IAPs) from human proteins with potent antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (45%) to Temporin-SHa. V=F: 15%. Discovered from the human unconventional myosin 1h protein by computer prediction. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC 32 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 21 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 32 uM). Inactive: T.rubrum (MIC 256 uM). In vitro Toxicity: human RBC: HC50 >128 uM. not hemo.lytic. Structure: it became helical after binding to lipids such as DMPG (88.6%) or DMPC (92.9%). Updated 8/2019; 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31386688", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2019 Aug 6;14(8):e0220656. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0220656. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03770", "source_id": "AP03770", "source_numeric_id": "03770", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03770", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Intragenic antimicrobial peptides (IAPs) from human proteins with potent antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antifungal, candidacidal, Hemolytic", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (52.38%) to P-04. L: 26%, K: 16%. Discovered from the human unconventional myosin 1h protein by computer prediction. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC 4 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 5.33 uM), fungi T. rubrum (MIC 32 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 8 uM). In vitro Toxicity: human RBC: HC50 64 uM. hemolytic. Structure: it became helical after binding to lipids. More helical in the presence of anionic DMPG (91.3%) than DMPC (50.8%).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31386688", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2019 Aug 6;14(8):e0220656. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0220656. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03771", "source_id": "AP03771", "source_numeric_id": "03771", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03771", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Intragenic antimicrobial peptides (IAPs) from human proteins with potent antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
